# Inner dict can shadow outer dict's type alias — lexical scoping.
# The outer ID alias is Integer; the inner nested dict shadows ID with String.
# The inner.inner value uses the shadowed String type.
[
  ID: [type Integer]
  outer: [@ID 42]
  nested: [
    ID: [type String]
    inner: [@ID "text"]
  ]
]
=== out
Dict({"ID": Dict({}), "outer": Int(42), "nested": Dict({"ID": Dict({}), "inner": String("text")})})
